## Lore

Tautons (pronounced taw-tuns) are giant humanoids with crocodile-like heads
and scorpion-like tails, once a major force among the minions of the
pantheon of Taut. The evil gods spent them recklessly in doomed campaigns, and
a race that once seemed about to destroy its ancient rivals, the ramen, has
fallen from tens of millions to perhaps 2.2 million, and has lost Set''s favor
through no fault of its own. That has made them bitter and crueler than ever.
Called to battle, they fight like relentless madmen with something to prove,
merciless above all toward the ramen and the Gods of Light, whom they blame
for their fate.

Their hatred borders on obsession. They will work with any dark force, and
they plot to draw the ramen and the Gods of Light into the war against the
Apocalypse demons, then strike at them from the shadows with hit-and-run
tactics while guarding the Four Horsemen. Set and the other dark gods find the
scheme amusing and give them a free hand; it may yet win back some of their
old standing among the minions of Taut.

Tautons prefer deserts and forests near water but may be found anywhere. A few
thousand serve Pharaoh Rama-Set; others are scattered across Africa. Their
allies are the Egyptian Gods of Darkness and other villains, the Four Horsemen
among them, and they tolerate and sometimes team up with the Worms of Taut.
They like all weapons, modern ones included, and love heavy energy weapons,
rail guns, power armor and techno-wizard gear, but prefer magic weapons,
vibro-blades and bladed weapons. Many wear heavy mega-damage body armor
(120 M.D.C.).

## GM Notes

A good or unprincipled tauton player character is, by the book, an aberration
and an outcast among its own kind. The snake metamorphosis has no statistics on
the page. The venom is meant for mega-damage beings, which is why it does so
much to an S.D.C. target.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'tauton');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'tauton';

